From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 02:47:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Stop allocating block positions on the light, AntiXray and
 path hot paths

Profiling a live server put BlockPosition at the top of the allocation
profile (97 MB/min, ~30% of everything), concentrated in a handful of
loops rather than spread across its 2400 call sites:

  - AntiXray walked six neighbours per recursion level via
    position.east()/up()/..., each of which allocates. It now recurses on
    plain int coordinates, with a matching World.isLoaded(x, y, z).
  - The light flood fill allocated a position per visited cell and six
    more per neighbour probe. World gains scalar getLightFor/setLightFor/
    getRawLight/areChunksLoaded/updateBrightness/c overloads and the two
    loops in World.c now work in ints. Chunk.updateSkylightNeighborHeight
    no longer builds a position per Y level.
  - PathfinderNormal.a ran for every candidate path point and allocated
    two positions each time; the scan position is now a per-thread
    scratch and the entity position is only materialized on the rare
    minecart-track branch.

Also caches EnumDirection.VALUES instead of calling values(), which
clones the array on every call - it showed up as 5 MB/min of its own.

Measured over 60s on a running server: BlockPosition 97.2 -> 0.5 MB,
MutableBlockPosition 31.5 -> 0, EnumDirection[] 5.1 -> 0, Vec3D
11.6 -> 0, PathPoint 8.2 -> 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>

